                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "74904b0e-493a-302d-af52-003143b3f974",
                        "entry_id": "5101cb7f-f875-389d-8e22-c35f5725a02e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative spelling of boggard (A bogey, a ghost)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aef60187-55eb-4b1f-9b4e-e3c94d4282af",
                                "sense_id": "74904b0e-493a-302d-af52-003143b3f974",
                                "text": "OH! Maeſter—ſtrange things late I've ſeen— / And oft has boggart-haunted been ! / I'm ſure I's falt when ſtory's-tauld, / 'Till blude run aw' through veins ſo cauld !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e79b13df-e07c-4660-9029-859725523628",
                                "sense_id": "74904b0e-493a-302d-af52-003143b3f974",
                                "text": "“[…]Are na ye shamed, ye weak gawly, that ye darena stir ower the threshold for fear of a boggart?”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "58cdd562-bb49-4bbc-9a90-7d3b78c69c4c",
                                "sense_id": "74904b0e-493a-302d-af52-003143b3f974",
                                "text": "Hoggart's Leap is a weird name, suggesting to the uninitiated some connection with a local tradition and a boggart or a barguest of Swaledale renown ; but I believe that Hoggart is really a family name, there being Hoggarth's Farm about two miles further up the Swale."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a0ddf5d1-0986-4847-bb1e-2ed4ba24ca49",
                                "sense_id": "74904b0e-493a-302d-af52-003143b3f974",
                                "text": "[…]but when it came to a question of standing up against the boggart of Arden—a thing, in the popular imagination, composed of neither flesh, blood, nor bones—even a physical giant had qualms and misgivings, and so had Joseph Wand."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e8314b2a-5e5f-3c3f-acfd-25849bae3722",
                        "entry_id": "5101cb7f-f875-389d-8e22-c35f5725a02e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A shapeshifting monster that feeds on fear."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "90a8b69e-94c3-4e65-85a1-fcd3a1fa0cdf",
                                "sense_id": "e8314b2a-5e5f-3c3f-acfd-25849bae3722",
                                "text": "\"A boogeyman,\" I said. \"Sometimes known as a boggle or a boggart. It's a weak form of phobophage - a fear-eater, mostly insubstantial.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54a974e3-be25-48db-b7ed-c2dcdfa7187a",
                                "sense_id": "e8314b2a-5e5f-3c3f-acfd-25849bae3722",
                                "text": "I pushed open the lid, half-expecting a Boggart to burst out of the trunk, taking the form of my worst nightmare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79ef5524-5891-41ea-8be0-d9a91c1d7694",
                                "sense_id": "e8314b2a-5e5f-3c3f-acfd-25849bae3722",
                                "text": "The boggart has brought you here because it hopes to feed off you like it has been trying to feed off me."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
